His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Senior Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, will lead a delegation to attend the 71st Session of the United Nations General Assembly (UNGA) from 20 to 25 September 2016 in New York.

On the Sidelines of the 71st Session of the UNGA, H.E. Senior Minister will attend the following meetings:

- The ASEAN Foreign Ministers’ Meeting with the President of the 71st UNGA and United Nations Secretary-General (AUMM);
- The Informal ASEAN-US Ministers’ Meeting;
- The Informal ASEAN Foreign Ministerial Meeting (IAMM);
- The Special Session of the ASEAN Foreign Ministers’ Meeting Focusing on Sustainable Development;
- The 3rd ASEAN-Pacific Alliance Ministerial Meeting.

H.E. Senior Minister PRAK Sokhonn will deliver his statement at the 71st Session of the UNGA under the theme “The Sustainable Development Goals: a Universal Push to Transform our World” that the world has been trying to translate into reality in order to achieve better living standard for all people around the globe.

In addition, Senior Minister PRAK Sokhonn will also have several bilateral meetings with Foreign Ministers and heads of delegation of some countries.

Phnom Penh, 15 September 2016

Press Release




 

Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN SEN, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia, will lead a high - level delegation to attend the following ASEAN Summit and Related Summits to be held from 06 to 08 September 2016 in Vientiane, Lao People’s Democratic Republic (PDR), at the invitation of His Excellency Dr. Thongloun SISOULITH, Prime Minister of Lao PDR:



- The 28th, 29th ASEAN Summits;
- The 19th ASEAN - China Summit to Commemorate the 25th Anniversary of ASEAN-China Dialogue Relations;
- The 19th ASEAN - Japan Summit;
- The 18th ASEAN - ROK Summit;
- The 19th ASEAN Plus Three Summit;
- The 2nd ASEAN - Australia Summit / First ASEAN - Australia Biennial Summit;
- The 7th ASEAN - United Nations Summit;
- The 14th ASEAN - India Summit;
- The 4th ASEAN - United States of America Summit;
- The 11th East Asia Summit;
- The ASEAN Leaders’ Interface with Representatives of ASEAN Inter-
Parliamentary Assembly;
- The ASEAN Leaders’ Interface with Representatives of ASEAN Youth;
- The ASEAN Leaders’ Interface with ASEAN Business Advisory Council;
- Joint Leaders’ Statement on the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP).

The delegation will include His Excellency PRAK Sokhonn, Senior Minister, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, His Excellency Dr. HANG Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, His Excellency PAN Sorasak, Minister of Commerce, and other members of the Royal Government of Cambodia.


During the 28th, 29th ASEAN Summit and related Summits, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN SEN, together with other ASEAN leaders, will sign the ASEAN Declaration on One ASEAN, One Response: ASEAN Responding to Disasters as One in the Region and Outside the Region.


On the sidelines of the 28th, 29th ASEAN summit, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN SEN will attend the following summits:


- ASEAN Business and Investment Summit 2016;
- 8th Mekong-Japan Summit.

In addition, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo HUN SEN will also hold bilateral meetings with Prime Ministers and heads of delegation of some countries.



Phnom Penh, 01 September 2016

As of 2026, His Excellency Noy Choumneanh, Ambassador Extraordinary and Plenipotentiary, serves as the Permanent Representative of the Kingdom of Cambodia to ASEAN. Prior to his current post, he was Deputy Director-General at the General Department of ASEAN, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation (MFAIC).
The ASEAN Charter provides for the establishment of the Committee of Permanent Representatives to ASEAN (CPR), which shall be constituted by the Permanent Representatives of ASEAN Member States at the rank of Ambassadors based in Jakarta. The Chairmanship of the Committee is in line with the annual rotation of ASEAN Chairmanship.
The CPR’s tasks may generally be categorized as follows:
Monitoring and implementing Leaders’ decisions;
Coordinating cross-pillar issues;
Strengthening relations with ASEAN’s external partners; and
Providing substantive and administrative direction and support to the ASEAN Secretariat.
Besides his role as the Permanent Representative of Cambodia to ASEAN, he is also the Representative of Cambodia and member of:
Initiative for ASEAN Integration (IAI) Task Force;
ASEAN Connectivity Coordinating Committee (ACCC);
Board of Trustees of the ASEAN Foundation;
Governing Council of
the ASEAN Institute for Peace and Reconciliation
; and
Joint Council of ASEAN-China Centre in Beijing.
